        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R47\") (value \"24k\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"222\") (name \"VOUTN\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"223\") (name \"VOUTP\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the MPN is used for sourcing, a 24Ω resistor would be installed across VOUTP and VOUTN instead of 24kΩ. Depending on the rail voltage, this could heavily load the output and overheat or damage the resistor or supply.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["J35", "J36", "U4", "U12"],
      "pins": ["J35.2", "J35.3", "J35.5", "J35.8", "J36.2", "J36.3", "J36.5", "J36.8", "U4.6", "U4.7", "U12.6", "U12.7"],
      "nets": ["/NET0002", "/NET0064", "/NET0153", "/NET0187"],
      "observed": "Both CAN transceiver pairs are routed to both connectors: U4's CANH/CANL nets reach pins 5/8 of J35 and J36, and U12's CANH/CANL nets reach pins 2/3 of J35 and J36.",
      "expected": "The specification describes two isolated CAN buses, each broken out on its own CAN interface connector. Each connector should carry its assigned bus rather than both bus pairs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller ... broken out on M12 circular connectors J2 (\"CAN Interface A\") and J13 (\"CAN Interface B\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"5\") (name \"/NET0002\") ... (node (ref \"J35\") (pin \"5\")) (node (ref \"J36\") (pin \"5\")) ... (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"CANH\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"42\") (name \"/NET0153\") ... (node (ref \"J35\") (pin \"8\")) (node (ref \"J36\") (pin \"8\")) ... (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"CANL\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"20\") (name \"/NET0064\") ... (node (ref \"J35\") (pin \"2\")) (node (ref \"J36\") (pin \"2\")) ... (node (ref \"U12\") (pin \"7\") (pinfunction \"CANH\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"45\") (name \"/NET0187\") ... (node (ref \"J35\") (pin \"3\")) (node (ref \"J36\") (pin \"3\")) ... (node (ref \"U12\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"CANL\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Both physical interfaces expose both CAN buses. Connecting devices or harnesses as if each connector were a separate bus could unintentionally couple the buses through external wiring or equipment.",
      "confidence": 0.79
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The BOM metadata for R47 conflicts with its stated 24k value and could result in a 24Ω part being fitted across the output rails. The netlist also routes both CAN bus pairs to both CAN connectors, contrary to the specification's separate-interface description."
}

